gpu_fetch_constant_caches (on by default, hot reload): what texture bindings and sampler parameters derive from a
texture fetch constant is kept in direct-mapped tables indexed by a hash of its six dwords: the binding key, signs and
host format swizzle (functions of the dwords), the textures last looked up for the key (reused while no texture was
destroyed and the scaled resolve generation is unchanged, or the key's scaled resolve state is still the texture's), and
the sampler parameters (also keyed on the binding's filter overrides and anisotropic_override). Saves the fetch
constant parse and the texture map lookup on most of the ~6,000 binding updates a frame, and the sampler parameter
computation on most of the ~3,000 a frame. Counters in the gpu_frame_stats log.

